Changes code from Helium's helium/core/ublock-setup-sources.patch, ublock-install-as-component.patch and
ublock-reconfigure-defaults.patch (GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors).

Helium's uBlock Origin component (blockjmkbacgjkknlgpkjjiijinjdanf) is neither built nor loaded: Ardia runs its own
uBlock Origin (fajbdaomknpkicfjcpipdmcpoamdmilh, packages/ardiacore/scripts/ubo.sh), loaded per profile with the
navigation hold, which keeps every user's filters and settings; with both, two engines would filter every request.
The build doesn't fetch Helium's uBO, so nothing depends on //third_party/ublock or its grit headers any more:
ComponentLoader has no AddUBlock, chrome_paks.gni packs no ublock_resources.pak, and the component allowlist and the
resource manager no longer list its resources. Its id is no longer pinned by default either, so no profile pins (and
syncs) an extension it doesn't have.

